    {
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "external_id": "d_c1_conflict_deescalation_scene_1",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-conflict-deescalation-01",
        "title": "Conflict De-escalation: part 1",
        "setting": "podcast planning call",
        "cefr": "C1",
        "topic": "polite-language",
        "characters": [
          "Noor",
          "Liam"
        ],
        "turns": [
          {
            "order": 1,
            "speaker": "Noor",
            "text": "Where do you think the strongest part of the case is?",
            "translation_fa": "فکر می‌کنی قوی‌ترین بخش استدلال کجاست؟"
          },
          {
            "order": 2,
            "speaker": "Liam",
            "text": "The immediate trigger was the email, but the friction had been building for weeks around unclear ownership.",
            "translation_fa": "محرک فوری ایمیل بود، ولی تنش چند هفته بود به خاطر مالکیت نامشخص کار جمع می‌شد."
          },
          {
            "order": 3,
            "speaker": "Noor",
            "text": "And where would you qualify it?",
            "translation_fa": "و کجاش رو با احتیاط یا قید بیشتری بیان می‌کردی؟"
          },
          {
            "order": 4,
            "speaker": "Liam",
            "text": "If we respond to the accusation with another accusation, we will probably escalate the part of the conflict that is easiest to avoid.",
            "translation_fa": "اگر به اتهام با اتهام جواب بدیم، احتمالاً همون بخشی از درگیری رو تشدید می‌کنیم که راحت‌تر می‌شه ازش جلوگیری کرد."
          }
        ],
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "external_id": "d_c1_conflict_deescalation_scene_2",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-conflict-deescalation-02",
        "title": "Conflict De-escalation: part 2",
        "setting": "project review",
        "cefr": "C1",
        "topic": "polite-language",
        "characters": [
          "Leila",
          "Adam"
        ],
        "turns": [
          {
            "order": 1,
            "speaker": "Leila",
            "text": "How would you put that more precisely?",
            "translation_fa": "چطور اون نکته رو دقیق‌تر بیان می‌کردی؟"
          },
          {
            "order": 2,
            "speaker": "Adam",
            "text": "I can acknowledge that the delay caused real pressure without accepting the claim that anyone acted in bad faith.",
            "translation_fa": "می‌تونم بپذیرم تأخیر فشار واقعی ایجاد کرده، بدون اینکه ادعای بدرفتاری عمدی رو قبول کنم."
          },
          {
            "order": 3,
            "speaker": "Leila",
            "text": "What distinction matters most here?",
            "translation_fa": "مهم‌ترین تمایز اینجا چیه؟"
          },
          {
            "order": 4,
            "speaker": "Adam",
            "text": "I would reframe the issue from 'who failed' to 'which handoff broke and how we prevent a repeat.'",
            "translation_fa": "مسئله رو از «چه کسی شکست خورد» به «کدوم تحویل کار خراب شد و چطور تکرارش نکنیم» تغییر می‌دم."
          }
        ],
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "external_id": "d_c1_conflict_deescalation_scene_3",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-conflict-deescalation-03",
        "title": "Conflict De-escalation: part 3",
        "setting": "quiet cafe",
        "cefr": "C1",
        "topic": "polite-language",
        "characters": [
          "Maya",
          "Daniel"
        ],
        "turns": [
          {
            "order": 1,
            "speaker": "Maya",
            "text": "What is the practical implication of that point?",
            "translation_fa": "پیامد عملی اون نکته چیه؟"
          },
          {
            "order": 2,
            "speaker": "Daniel",
            "text": "De-escalation does not mean tolerating personal attacks; a clear boundary can make the conversation safer and more productive.",
            "translation_fa": "تنش‌زدایی یعنی حمله شخصی رو تحمل کنیم نیست؛ مرز روشن می‌تونه گفتگو رو امن‌تر و سازنده‌تر کنه."
          },
          {
            "order": 3,
            "speaker": "Maya",
            "text": "Does the evidence justify going that far?",
            "translation_fa": "آیا شواهد واقعاً چنین نتیجه‌ای رو توجیه می‌کنه؟"
          },
          {
            "order": 4,
            "speaker": "Daniel",
            "text": "A specific apology can defuse tension more effectively than a vague attempt to move on quickly.",
            "translation_fa": "یک عذرخواهی مشخص می‌تونه خیلی مؤثرتر از تلاش مبهم برای زود عبور کردن، تنش رو خنثی کنه."
          }
        ],
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
